      "side": 1,
      "message": "Possible alternative:\n\n```\npub enum PowerState {\n    StandbyOrRetention(u32),\n    PowerOff(u32),\n}\n```\n\nThen:\n\n```\nimpl TryFrom\u003cu32\u003e for PowerState {\n    type Error \u003d Error;\n\n    fn try_from(value: u32) -\u003e Result\u003cSelf, Self::Error\u003e {\n        const MBZ_BITS: u32 \u003d 0xb000_0000;\n        if value \u0026 MBZ_BITS !\u003d 0 {\n            return Err(Error::InvalidPowerState(value));\n        }\n        \n        let v \u003d value \u0026 0x0fff_ffff;\n        Ok(if (value \u0026 0x4000_0000) \u003d\u003d 0 {\n            PowerState::StandbyOrRetention(v)\n        } else {\n            PowerState::PowerOff(v)\n        })\n    }\n}\n```\n\nJudging by the results I got from `std::mem::size_of`, I think our 2 approaches are the same in the end, at least for object representation. So, it\u0027d only be a source code parsimony thing. Up to you!",
